  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2008-p25.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "-1 If \\(k<18\\), then we can pair \\(\\cos \\left(\\frac{k \\pi}{18}\\right)\\) with \\(\\cos \\left(\\frac{(18-k) \\pi}{18}\\right)\\), and these two terms sum to 0 . If \\(k>18\\), then the pair \\(\\cos \\left(\\frac{k \\pi}{18}\\right)\\) and \\(\\cos \\left(\\frac{(36-k) \\pi}{18}\\right)\\) also sums to 0 . So, the only term in this series that is left over is \\(\\cos \\left(\\frac{18 \\pi}{18}\\right)=-1\\).",
